{%- comment -%}
  Read a numeric value out of a product tag: `rating:4.7` -> 4.7

    {%- capture r -%}{% render 'tagval', tags: product.tags, key: 'rating' %}{%- endcapture -%}

  WHY TAGS. The ratings, review counts and sold figures are written as
  metafields by the product importer, which is the right home for them - a
  reviews app installed later takes the same fields over instead of fighting
  them. But on this store not one of the 22 live products was showing a rating:
  every card rendered the empty `card__rating--none` row, because Shopify's CSV
  importer had written no metafield at all.

  Tags always import. So the numbers now travel BOTH ways and the theme prefers
  the metafield, falling back to the tag. Nothing is invented either way - if
  both are missing the row still renders empty, exactly as before.

  Outputs nothing at all when the tag is absent, so the caller's `!= blank`
  test behaves.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign want = key | append: ':'
  for t in tags
    if t contains want
      assign v = t | remove_first: want | strip
      echo v
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}
